{
  "description": "config.v2 §2.8: a set's or an extend's confirm_s, the owner's floor, the instant the owner received the call and the deployment epoch -> the window, the deadline and its code; and a reach set's apply_at as the device states it -> the apply_at the owner writes and its code. Written by an independent reading of the text (Python, standard library), checked, never blessed. confirm_s and floor_s are whole seconds from 1 to 65535; received and device_apply_at are milliseconds since the Unix epoch on the owner's clock; epoch is E in seconds. expect.window_s is max(confirm_s, floor_s); expect.deadline is received plus window_s seconds, rounded up to the next whole second when it falls between two, so a window is never shorter than asked; expect.deadline_code is the Record's time field, (deadline - 1000 E) / 1000 (core §7.6); expect.apply_at and apply_at_code round the device's instant up the same way. The owner acts at the instant it states: the undo at deadline, the apply at apply_at.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "note": "the window asked for, above the floor, received on a second",
      "op": "set",
      "confirm_s": 120,
      "floor_s": 10,
      "received": 1762000000000,
      "epoch": 0,
      "expect": {
        "window_s": 120,
        "deadline": 1762000120000,
        "deadline_code": 1762000120
      }
    },
